  "id": "directional-test",
  "term": "directional test",
  "definition": "A directional test is a significance test that calculates probability for results as extreme as the observed one in only one specified direction, such as values larger than the null-hypothesized parameter. It is the same as a one-tailed test or one-tailed probability.",
